  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 105 PM CDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nHigh pressure continues through much of the extended period. Long \nrange models seem persistent in showing an eventual displacement and \nweakening of the upper ridge that could lead to height falls and \noverall temperature relief. However, these changes are still several \ndays out, so models will need more temporal consistency before \nconfidence increases regarding a pattern shift. In the meantime, hot \ntemperatures prevail over the entire CWA through much of the new \nweek. 100's will continue areawide with some models suggesting \ntemperatures can meet or exceed 105 degrees in the eastern half of \nour CWA. PoPs also stay low through the first half of the new week, \nbut if high pressure does elongate and shift east of the High \nPlains, favorable southerly steering flow will advect moisture into \nthe area and increase PoPs across the entire region by the end of\nthe week. \n\nRangel",
